# SPIRV-Cross Notes

## What I was trying to do
Convert SPIR-V into GLSL, MSL, HLSL, and other shading languages.

## What I started with
- spirv-cross GitHub repo
- sample shaders

## What each part does
- Compiler: converts SPIR-V to target language
- Reflection: tells you what resources exist

## What happened
- Cross-compiling works well.
- Reflection is super useful for engine code.

## What confused me
- Some languages need special options.
- Resource binding rules differ per backend.

## What I want to try next
- Convert Vulkan shaders to GLSL and HLSL.
- Test reflection with my own shaders.

## Random thoughts
SPIRV-Cross is basically the “translator” of the GPU world.
